    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="46">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 46</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="46" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="108" ed="#liebermann"/>XC. Ðonne mon monnan betyhð, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he ceap forstele<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#Ine_46.lnote.oe.30"/> oððe forstolenne gefeormie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#Ine_46.lnote.oe.31"/>, þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> sceal he be LX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Ine_46.lnote.oe.32"/> hida onsacan þære þiefðe, gif he aðwyrðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#Ine_46.lnote.oe.33"/> bið.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="46" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="108" ed="#liebermann"/>XC. Þonne mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_46.lnote.oe.7"/> mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Ine_46.lnote.oe.18"/> betyhð, ðæt he ceap forstæle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Ine_46.lnote.oe.19"/> oððe forstolenne gefeormige<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_46.lnote.oe.20"/>, þonne scel<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_46.lnote.oe.15"/> he be LX hida onsacan þære ðyfðe, gif he aðwyrðe biþ.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="46" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="108" ed="#liebermann"/>Be staltihlan. Ðonne mon mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_46.lnote.oe.6"/> betyhð þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he ceap forstǽle oððe forstolene gefeormie, ðonne sceal he be syxti hída ætsacan ðære ðeofðe, gyf he andwyrde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_46.lnote.oe.3"/> bið.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="46" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="109" ed="#liebermann"/>Quando aliquis homo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Ine_46.lnote.oe.24"/> inculpatur, quod captale furatus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Ine_46.lnote.oe.25"/> sit (furtum fecerit) uel furtiuum aliquid firmauerit, tunc debet per LX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#Ine_46.lnote.oe.26"/> hidas (id est per<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#Ine_46.lnote.oe.27"/> sex homines) abnegare ipsum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#Ine_46.lnote.oe.28"/> furtum, si iuramento dignus sit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="50" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be staltihlan.] Ðonne mon monnan<ptr type="editorNote" n="18" target="#Ine_46.attnote.fn.18"/> betyhð, þæt he ceap forstele oððe forstolenne gefeormie, þonne sceal he be LX hida onsacan<ptr type="editorNote" n="19" target="#Ine_46.attnote.fn.19"/> þære þiefðe, gif he aðwyrðe<ptr type="editorNote" n="20" target="#Ine_46.attnote.fn.20"/> bið.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="47" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="410" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{XC} Ðonne mon monnan betyhð, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he ceap forstele oððe forstolenne gefeormie, þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> sceal he be LX hida onsacan þære þiefðe, gif he aðwyrðe bið.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="109" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn man jemanden<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_46.lnote.de.1"/> bezichtigt, dass er Vieh stehle oder gestohlenes beherberge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_46.lnote.de.2"/>, dann soll er durch [Eid von] 60 Hiden<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_46.lnote.de.3"/> von dem Diebstahle sich frei schwören, wenn er eideswürdig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_46.lnote.de.4"/> ist.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone is accused of stealing livestock or harbouring stolen [livestock], then he is to swear himself free of the theft by [an oath of] 60 hides, if he is worthy of an oath.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="51" ed="#attenborough"/>When one man charges another with stealing cattle, or harbouring stolen cattle, he shall deny [the charge of] theft by [an oath of] 60 hides, if he is allowed to produce an oath<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_46.attnote.n.1"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="405" ed="#whitelock"/>When anyone accuses a man that he stole cattle or received stolen cattle, he must deny the theft by [an oath of] 60 hides, if he is entitled to give an oath.<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Ine_46.whinote.n.2"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="411" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If a man is accused of the theft of livestock or of supplying stolen [livestock] with fodder, then he must deny the theft by [an oath of] sixty hides, if he is oathworthy.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="278"><ref target="clause:Af_9-2">Af 9.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="405"><ref target="clause:Ine_37">Ine 37</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="305"><ref target="clause:IIAs_1">II As 1–1.5</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_46.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh.</hi> ann <hi rend="italic">über der Zeile</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ann above the line in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_46.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_46.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">109</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur aus Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only from Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_46.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">109</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> furtum fe. <hi rend="italic">übrige;</hi> f. f. uel <hi rend="italic">überspringt R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond; furtum fe. the others; f. f. uel omitted by R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_46.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">109</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">XL <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">XL R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_46.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">109</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cum s. (sexaginta <hi rend="italic">Co</hi>) hominibus <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cum s. (sexaginta Co) hominibus Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_46.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">109</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">i. f. <hi rend="italic">nur aus Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">i. f. only from Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_46.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_46.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">dahinter Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">erasure after it</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_46.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">æ <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">æ on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_46.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">zweites</hi> e <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">second e on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_46.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> sceal</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to sceal</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_46.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-stæle <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-stæle Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_46.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-mige <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-mige Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_46.lnote.oe.32" n="32" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">syxtig hyda ætsa. ðær ðeofþe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">syxtig hyda ætsa. ðær ðeofþe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_46.lnote.oe.33" n="33" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rþ <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rþ Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_46.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">H cor. B modernisieren</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">H cor. B modernise</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_46.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Hehler 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Hehler 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_46.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">6 Freie richtig Q, wenn Abendmahlsgänger; <hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> Eideshufen 9</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">6 freemen Q, rightly, if they are communicants; <hi rend="italic">see Gl</hi> Eideshufen 9</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_46.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> eidesfähig 3—6; bescholten 1b</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> eidesfähig 3—6; bescholten 1b</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_46.attnote.fn.18" n="18" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">50</biblScope></bibl><label>monnan</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">mon</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_46.attnote.fn.19" n="19" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">50</biblScope></bibl><label>onsacan</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ætsacan</hi>. B.</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The number 19 is printed 2 times on the page (46, 46.2), with one footnote.</note></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_46.attnote.fn.20" n="20" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">50</biblScope></bibl><label>aðwyrðe</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">andwyrde</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_46.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">190</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">For the loss of the right to produce an oath see I Edw. cap. 3; II As. cap. 25; II Can. cap. 36.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Ine_46.whinote.n.2" n="2" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">405</biblScope></bibl><label>oath</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">i.e. if he has not forfeited his right to swear an oath by previous conviction for crime, especially perjury.</seg></note>
